#
# The EXACT output of the native producer math::producers::proof_lift (dogfooded — this
# fixture IS what the producer emits, byte for byte after the SPDX header block).
# proof_lift runs the shipped executable proof front-end, gmeow_math_lift::proof::lift —
# the same entrypoint the `gmeow` CLI calls — over the real committed artifact
# crates/math-lift/fixtures/theorem-subclass.tstp, embedded in the binary at compile
# time, and mints under the producer namespace. Nothing here is hand-authored: every
# triple was read by the TSTP annotated-formula parser and lifted.
#
# The run is a math:ProofIngestRun carrying the four ingest-frame obligations (a retained
# logic:loadBearing math:parseSource witness, logic:instantiatesSchema,
# logic:instantiatesPlan, and a math:ingestCorrespondence whose logic:Correspondence
# holds the whole law spine), and a structured math: codomain of 29 nodes, each
# gmeow:wasGeneratedBy the run — a non-empty lift, clean under math:UnliftableIngest.
# This is the one bridge whose rung is a SECTION/RETRACTION (logic:SectionRetraction /
# logic:ExactPreservation / logic:Equiv / logic:Crisp, logic:mnemomorphic true): the lift
# carries every step name, inference rule, parent edge, and rendered conclusion, so the
# derivation reconstructs from the lift plus its witness.
#
# Drift is a loud failure: crates/math/tests/lift_fixture_drift.rs regenerates the
# producer and byte-compares against this file.

